{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Submitted rtl_source axil_timer.v and testbench axil_timer_tb.v for the platform's lint, simulation and synthesis checks. No formal_spec is submitted.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "design_note", "title": "axil_timer implementation decisions", "summary": "The RTL follows the channel, timer-ordering, decode and reset plan of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1], which implements [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1] for [requirement:req-2b2b91a584]. Channels: aw_held and w_held hold a lone address or data; awready = !aw_held && !bvalid; wready = !w_held && !bvalid; do_write fires when both halves are present; arready = !rvalid. Timer priorities come from one combinational next-state block, evaluated in this order: count step, then EXPIRED clear followed by set, then CTRL, then LOAD byte merge. count_end = en && count <= 1. The decode checks addr[1:0] == 0 and that the bits from 4 up are zero; a generate block keeps the zero-width case out at ADDR_WIDTH 4. irq = expired && ie. One recorded deviation: the held address, data and strobe registers are reset, although the microarchitecture says they need no reset. This keeps every flop reset and changes no visible behavior."}], "files": [{"path": "axil_timer.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "axil_timer RTL", "summary": "Synthesizable Verilog-2001 for the AXI4-Lite timer of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1], structured as in [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1]. It has a synchronous active-low reset on every flop, default assignments in every combinational block, a case statement with a default branch, and no delays or system tasks. Design-intent assertions on the channel invariants are guarded by ifdef FORMAL. No .sby is submitted, so nothing checks those assertions yet.", "entry": "axil_timer"}, {"path": "axil_timer_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "axil_timer self-checking testbench", "summary": "Directed self-checking testbench for the section 8 list of [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.interface-spec.a1]. It runs an ADDR_WIDTH 8 instance and an ADDR_WIDTH 4 instance in lockstep, with a per-cycle output comparator; the 4-bit lane is gated off while offsets 0x10 to 0xFF are tested. It counts rising edges and times every count end from the edge the starting write took effect, as [artifact:prj-97dea43f5b.microarchitecture.a1] requires. It lands a STATUS clear exactly on a periodic count-end edge, and lands CTRL writes with EN 1 and with EN 0 on count-end edges. It also covers reset during a count with pending B and R responses, and checks that a held address does not survive reset. Every failure is reported with $error. It prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once and then calls $finish.", "entry": "axil_timer_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["I have not run lint, simulation, synthesis or formal on these files. Whether they pass is unknown until the platform runs them.", "No formal_spec (.sby) is submitted. The formal proof required by interface_spec section 8 and the axil_timer.sby and axil_timer_aw8.sby files in the microarchitecture verification plan are still open. A follow-up task is needed for them.", "The testbench assumes Verilator runs with timing support (--timing or --binary), because it uses # delays and event controls.", "The expected count-end edges in the testbench are calculated by hand from the specification's timing rule: a count started on edge E with LOAD N ends on edge E+N, and a LOAD of 0 counts as 1."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Known deviations: (1) The held AW and W registers are reset, which the microarchitecture marks as unnecessary. This is harmless. (2) The next-state block assigns some variables more than once to get last-assignment-wins priority, as the microarchitecture specifies. This goes beyond the default-then-override style rule. (3) The interface spec's formal proof item is not covered here, because the task asks only for rtl_source and testbench. (4) A simultaneous read and write on the same clock is not driven in the directed tests, but the two directions are independent in the RTL. Under Verilator, the default runtime error limit stops the simulation at the first $error. A failing run therefore ends without printing a verdict, and it still counts as a failure."}

=== FILE: axil_timer.v ===
// axil_timer: 32-bit down-counting timer, one-shot and periodic modes,
// level interrupt, behind an AXI4-Lite subordinate port.
// Implements interface_spec.md following microarchitecture.md.
`default_nettype none

module axil_timer #(
    parameter integer ADDR_WIDTH = 4
) (
    input  wire                  aclk,
    input  wire                  aresetn,
    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] s_axil_awaddr,
    input  wire                  s_axil_awvalid,
    output wire                  s_axil_awready,
    input  wire [31:0]           s_axil_wdata,
    input  wire [3:0]            s_axil_wstrb,
    input  wire                  s_axil_wvalid,
    output wire                  s_axil_wready,
    output reg  [1:0]            s_axil_bresp,
    output reg                   s_axil_bvalid,
    input  wire                  s_axil_bready,
    input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] s_axil_araddr,
    input  wire                  s_axil_arvalid,
    output wire                  s_axil_arready,
    output reg  [31:0]           s_axil_rdata,
    output reg  [1:0]            s_axil_rresp,
    output reg                   s_axil_rvalid,
    input  wire                  s_axil_rready,
    output wire                  irq
);

    localparam [1:0] RESP_OKAY   = 2'b00;
    localparam [1:0] RESP_SLVERR = 2'b10;
    localparam [1:0] IDX_CTRL    = 2'd0;
    localparam [1:0] IDX_LOAD    = 2'd1;
    localparam [1:0] IDX_COUNT   = 2'd2;
    localparam [1:0] IDX_STATUS  = 2'd3;

    // Channel state
    reg                  aw_held;
    reg                  w_held;
    reg [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] awaddr_q;
    reg [31:0]           wdata_q;
    reg [3:0]            wstrb_q;

    // Timer state
    reg        en_q;
    reg        ie_q;
    reg        mode_q;
    reg        expired_q;
    reg [31:0] load_q;
    reg [31:0] count_q;

    // Timer next state
    reg        en_d;
    reg        ie_d;
    reg        mode_d;
    reg        expired_d;
    reg [31:0] load_d;
    reg [31:0] count_d;

    // Read mux
    reg [31:0] rd_val;
    reg [1:0]  rd_resp;

    assign s_axil_awready = !aw_held && !s_axil_bvalid;
    assign s_axil_wready  = !w_held && !s_axil_bvalid;
    assign s_axil_arready = !s_axil_rvalid;

    wire aw_hs = s_axil_awvalid && s_axil_awready;
    wire w_hs  = s_axil_wvalid && s_axil_wready;
    wire ar_hs = s_axil_arvalid && s_axil_arready;

    wire do_write = (aw_held || aw_hs) && (w_held || w_hs);

    wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0] wr_addr = aw_held ? awaddr_q : s_axil_awaddr;
    wire [31:0]           wr_data = w_held ? wdata_q : s_axil_wdata;
    wire [3:0]            wr_strb = w_held ? wstrb_q : s_axil_wstrb;

    // Address decode: word aligned and below 0x10.
    wire wr_hi_zero;
    wire rd_hi_zero;
    generate
        if (ADDR_WIDTH > 4) begin : g_wide
            assign wr_hi_zero = ~|wr_addr[ADDR_WIDTH-1:4];
            assign rd_hi_zero = ~|s_axil_araddr[ADDR_WIDTH-1:4];
        end else begin : g_narrow
            assign wr_hi_zero = 1'b1;
            assign rd_hi_zero = 1'b1;
        end
    endgenerate

    wire       wr_mapped = (wr_addr[1:0] == 2'b00) && wr_hi_zero;
    wire [1:0] wr_idx    = wr_addr[3:2];
    wire       rd_mapped = (s_axil_araddr[1:0] == 2'b00) && rd_hi_zero;
    wire [1:0] rd_idx    = s_axil_araddr[3:2];

    wire wr_ctrl  = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == IDX_CTRL) && wr_strb[0];
    wire wr_load  = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == IDX_LOAD);
    wire wr_clear = do_write && wr_mapped && (wr_idx == IDX_STATUS) &&
                    wr_strb[0] && wr_data[0];
    wire wr_err   = !wr_mapped || (wr_idx == IDX_COUNT);

    wire count_end = en_q && (count_q <= 32'd1);

    assign irq = expired_q && ie_q;

    // Read data and response for the address presented on AR.
    always @(*) begin
        rd_val  = 32'd0;
        rd_resp = RESP_OKAY;
        if (!rd_mapped) begin
            rd_resp = RESP_SLVERR;
        end else begin
            case (rd_idx)
                IDX_CTRL:   rd_val = {29'd0, mode_q, ie_q, en_q};
                IDX_LOAD:   rd_val = load_q;
                IDX_COUNT:  rd_val = count_q;
                IDX_STATUS: rd_val = {31'd0, expired_q};
                default:    rd_val = 32'd0;
            endcase
        end
    end

    // Timer next state. Later assignments win, which gives the
    // specification's priorities (microarchitecture section 2).
    always @(*) begin
        en_d      = en_q;
        ie_d      = ie_q;
        mode_d    = mode_q;
        expired_d = expired_q;
        load_d    = load_q;
        count_d   = count_q;

        // 1. Count step
        if (en_q) begin
            if (count_end) begin
                if (mode_q) begin
                    count_d = load_q;
                end else begin
                    count_d = 32'd0;
                    en_d    = 1'b0;
                end
            end else begin
                count_d = count_q - 32'd1;
            end
        end

        // 2. EXPIRED: clear, then set (a count end beats a clear)
        if (wr_clear) begin
            expired_d = 1'b0;
        end
        if (count_end) begin
            expired_d = 1'b1;
        end

        // 3. CTRL write wins for EN and COUNT
        if (wr_ctrl) begin
            ie_d   = wr_data[1];
            mode_d = wr_data[2];
            if (wr_data[0]) begin
                en_d    = 1'b1;
                count_d = load_q;
            end else begin
                en_d = 1'b0;
            end
        end

        // 4. LOAD byte merge
        if (wr_load) begin
            if (wr_strb[0]) load_d[7:0]   = wr_data[7:0];
            if (wr_strb[1]) load_d[15:8]  = wr_data[15:8];
            if (wr_strb[2]) load_d[23:16] = wr_data[23:16];
            if (wr_strb[3]) load_d[31:24] = wr_data[31:24];
        end
    end

    always @(posedge aclk) begin
        if (!aresetn) begin
            aw_held       <= 1'b0;
            w_held        <= 1'b0;
            awaddr_q      <= {ADDR_WIDTH{1'b0}};
            wdata_q       <= 32'd0;
            wstrb_q       <= 4'd0;
            s_axil_bvalid <= 1'b0;
            s_axil_bresp  <= RESP_OKAY;
            s_axil_rvalid <= 1'b0;
            s_axil_rdata  <= 32'd0;
            s_axil_rresp  <= RESP_OKAY;
            en_q          <= 1'b0;
            ie_q          <= 1'b0;
            mode_q        <= 1'b0;
            expired_q     <= 1'b0;
            load_q        <= 32'd0;
            count_q       <= 32'd0;
        end else begin
            if (do_write) begin
                aw_held <= 1'b0;
                w_held  <= 1'b0;
            end else begin
                if (aw_hs) begin
                    aw_held  <= 1'b1;
                    awaddr_q <= s_axil_awaddr;
                end
                if (w_hs) begin
                    w_held  <= 1'b1;
                    wdata_q <= s_axil_wdata;
                    wstrb_q <= s_axil_wstrb;
                end
            end

            if (do_write) begin
                s_axil_bvalid <= 1'b1;
                s_axil_bresp  <= wr_err ? RESP_SLVERR : RESP_OKAY;
            end else if (s_axil_bready) begin
                s_axil_bvalid <= 1'b0;
            end

            if (ar_hs) begin
                s_axil_rvalid <= 1'b1;
                s_axil_rdata  <= rd_val;
                s_axil_rresp  <= rd_resp;
            end else if (s_axil_rready) begin
                s_axil_rvalid <= 1'b0;
            end

            en_q      <= en_d;
            ie_q      <= ie_d;
            mode_q    <= mode_d;
            expired_q <= expired_d;
            load_q    <= load_d;
            count_q   <= count_d;
        end
    end

`ifdef FORMAL
    // Design-intent channel invariants, valid once a reset has been seen.
    reg f_rst_seen = 1'b0;
    always @(posedge aclk) begin
        if (!aresetn) begin
            f_rst_seen <= 1'b1;
        end
    end

    always @(*) begin
        if (f_rst_seen) begin
            assert (!(aw_held && w_held));
            assert (!(s_axil_bvalid && (aw_held || w_held)));
            assert (!(s_axil_bvalid && do_write));
            assert (!(s_axil_rvalid && ar_hs));
        end
    end
`endif

endmodule

`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: axil_timer_tb.v ===
// axil_timer_tb: self-checking testbench for axil_timer.
// dut8 (ADDR_WIDTH 8) and dut4 (ADDR_WIDTH 4) run in lockstep; a comparator
// checks that their outputs agree whenever the 4-bit lane is enabled.

`define CHECK(c_, m_) \
    begin \
        if (c_) passed = passed + 1; \
        else begin \
            failed = failed + 1; \
            $error("FAIL at %0t: %0s", $time, m_); \
        end \
    end

`define CHECK_EQ(g_, e_, m_) \
    begin \
        if ((g_) === (e_)) passed = passed + 1; \
        else begin \
            failed = failed + 1; \
            $error("FAIL at %0t: %0s: got %0h expected %0h", $time, m_, g_, e_); \
        end \
    end

`define READ_EXPECT(a_, d_, r_, m_) \
    begin \
        axi_read(a_, 0); \
        `CHECK_EQ(rd_data, d_, m_) \
        `CHECK_EQ(rd_resp, r_, m_) \
    end

module axil_timer_tb;

    localparam [7:0] A_CTRL   = 8'h00;
    localparam [7:0] A_LOAD   = 8'h04;
    localparam [7:0] A_COUNT  = 8'h08;
    localparam [7:0] A_STATUS = 8'h0C;
    localparam [1:0] OKAY     = 2'b00;
    localparam [1:0] SLVERR   = 2'b10;

    reg aclk = 1'b0;
    always #5 aclk = ~aclk;

    reg        aresetn;
    reg  [7:0] awaddr;
    reg        awvalid;
    reg [31:0] wdata;
    reg  [3:0] wstrb;
    reg        wvalid;
    reg        bready;
    reg  [7:0] araddr;
    reg        arvalid;
    reg        rready;
    reg        lane4_en;

    wire        awready8, wready8, bvalid8, arready8, rvalid8, irq8;
    wire  [1:0] bresp8, rresp8;
    wire [31:0] rdata8;
    wire        awready4, wready4, bvalid4, arready4, rvalid4, irq4;
    wire  [1:0] bresp4, rresp4;
    wire [31:0] rdata4;

    axil_timer #(.ADDR_WIDTH(8)) dut8 (
        .aclk           (aclk),
        .aresetn        (aresetn),
        .s_axil_awaddr  (awaddr),
        .s_axil_awvalid (awvalid),
        .s_axil_awready (awready8),
        .s_axil_wdata   (wdata),
        .s_axil_wstrb   (wstrb),
        .s_axil_wvalid  (wvalid),
        .s_axil_wready  (wready8),
        .s_axil_bresp   (bresp8),
        .s_axil_bvalid  (bvalid8),
        .s_axil_bready  (bready),
        .s_axil_araddr  (araddr),
        .s_axil_arvalid (arvalid),
        .s_axil_arready (arready8),
        .s_axil_rdata   (rdata8),
        .s_axil_rresp   (rresp8),
        .s_axil_rvalid  (rvalid8),
        .s_axil_rready  (rready),
        .irq            (irq8)
    );

    axil_timer #(.ADDR_WIDTH(4)) dut4 (
        .aclk           (aclk),
        .aresetn        (aresetn),
        .s_axil_awaddr  (awaddr[3:0]),
        .s_axil_awvalid (awvalid & lane4_en),
        .s_axil_awready (awready4),
        .s_axil_wdata   (wdata),
        .s_axil_wstrb   (wstrb),
        .s_axil_wvalid  (wvalid & lane4_en),
        .s_axil_wready  (wready4),
        .s_axil_bresp   (bresp4),
        .s_axil_bvalid  (bvalid4),
        .s_axil_bready  (bready),
        .s_axil_araddr  (araddr[3:0]),
        .s_axil_arvalid (arvalid & lane4_en),
        .s_axil_arready (arready4),
        .s_axil_rdata   (rdata4),
        .s_axil_rresp   (rresp4),
        .s_axil_rvalid  (rvalid4),
        .s_axil_rready  (rready),
        .irq            (irq4)
    );

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;

    // Rising-edge counter
    integer edge_cnt = 0;
    always @(posedge aclk) edge_cnt <= edge_cnt + 1;

    // irq monitor: records the edge after which irq rose
    integer irq_rise_cnt  = 0;
    integer irq_fall_cnt  = 0;
    integer irq_rise_edge = -1;
    reg     irq_prev      = 1'b0;
    always @(negedge aclk) begin
        if (irq8 && !irq_prev) begin
            irq_rise_cnt  = irq_rise_cnt + 1;
            irq_rise_edge = edge_cnt;
        end
        if (!irq8 && irq_prev) begin
            irq_fall_cnt = irq_fall_cnt + 1;
        end
        irq_prev = irq8;
    end

    // Lane comparator
    integer lane_cmp      = 0;
    integer lane_mismatch = 0;
    always @(negedge aclk) begin
        if (lane4_en && aresetn) begin
            lane_cmp = lane_cmp + 1;
            if ((awready4 !== awready8) || (wready4 !== wready8) ||
                (arready4 !== arready8) || (bvalid4 !== bvalid8) ||
                (rvalid4 !== rvalid8) || (irq4 !== irq8) ||
                (bvalid8 && (bresp4 !== bresp8)) ||
                (rvalid8 && ((rdata4 !== rdata8) || (rresp4 !== rresp8)))) begin
                lane_mismatch = lane_mismatch + 1;
                $error("FAIL at %0t: ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8 lanes disagree", $time);
            end
        end
    end

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Tasks: each starts and ends just after a falling edge.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    task idle;
        input integer n;
        begin
            repeat (n) @(negedge aclk);
        end
    endtask

    task wait_until;
        input integer target;
        begin
            while (edge_cnt < target) @(negedge aclk);
        end
    endtask

    reg [1:0] wr_resp;
    integer   wr_edge;

    // order: 0 address and data together, 1 address first, 2 data first
    task axi_write;
        input [7:0]   addr;
        input [31:0]  data;
        input [3:0]   strb;
        input integer order;
        input integer gap;
        input integer bp;
        reg     aw_take;
        reg     w_take;
        reg     aw_done;
        reg     w_done;
        integer gap_left;
        integer guard;
        integer k;
        begin
            awaddr   = addr;
            wdata    = data;
            wstrb    = strb;
            aw_done  = 1'b0;
            w_done   = 1'b0;
            gap_left = gap;
            guard    = 0;
            if (order != 2) awvalid = 1'b1;
            if (order != 1) wvalid = 1'b1;
            while (!(aw_done && w_done) && (guard < 100)) begin
                aw_take = awvalid && awready8;
                w_take  = wvalid && wready8;
                @(negedge aclk);
                guard = guard + 1;
                if (aw_take) begin
                    awvalid = 1'b0;
                    aw_done = 1'b1;
                end
                if (w_take) begin
                    wvalid = 1'b0;
                    w_done = 1'b1;
                end
                if (aw_done && !w_done && !wvalid) begin
                    `CHECK(!awready8, "awready low while an address is held")
                    `CHECK(!bvalid8, "no write response before the data")
                    if (gap_left == 0) wvalid = 1'b1;
                    else gap_left = gap_left - 1;
                end
                if (w_done && !aw_done && !awvalid) begin
                    `CHECK(!wready8, "wready low while data is held")
                    `CHECK(!bvalid8, "no write response before the address")
                    if (gap_left == 0) awvalid = 1'b1;
                    else gap_left = gap_left - 1;
                end
            end
            `CHECK(aw_done && w_done, "write handshakes complete")
            `CHECK(bvalid8, "bvalid on the edge after the write completes")
            wr_edge = edge_cnt;
            wr_resp = bresp8;
            for (k = 0; k < bp; k = k + 1) begin
                @(negedge aclk);
                `CHECK(bvalid8, "bvalid held under back-pressure")
                `CHECK_EQ(bresp8, wr_resp, "bresp stable under back-pressure")
                `CHECK(!awready8 && !wready8, "no write accepted while a response waits")
            end
            bready = 1'b1;
            @(negedge aclk);
            bready = 1'b0;
            `CHECK(!bvalid8, "bvalid drops after the handshake")
        end
    endtask

    reg [31:0] rd_data;
    reg [1:0]  rd_resp;
    integer    rd_edge;

    task axi_read;
        input [7:0]   addr;
        input integer bp;
        integer guard;
        integer k;
        begin
            araddr  = addr;
            arvalid = 1'b1;
            guard   = 0;
            while (!arready8 && (guard < 100)) begin
                @(negedge aclk);
                guard = guard + 1;
            end
            @(negedge aclk);
            arvalid = 1'b0;
            rd_edge = edge_cnt;
            `CHECK(rvalid8, "rvalid on the edge after the address")
            rd_data = rdata8;
            rd_resp = rresp8;
            for (k = 0; k < bp; k = k + 1) begin
                @(negedge aclk);
                `CHECK(rvalid8, "rvalid held under back-pressure")
                `CHECK_EQ(rdata8, rd_data, "rdata stable under back-pressure")
                `CHECK_EQ(rresp8, rd_resp, "rresp stable under back-pressure")
                `CHECK(!arready8, "no read accepted while a response waits")
            end
            rready = 1'b1;
            @(negedge aclk);
            rready = 1'b0;
            `CHECK(!rvalid8, "rvalid drops after the handshake")
        end
    endtask

    task expect_rise;
        input integer edge_exp;
        input integer cnt_exp;
        begin
            wait_until(edge_exp + 2);
            `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, cnt_exp, "number of interrupt rises")
            `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_edge, edge_exp, "edge on which the count ended")
        end
    endtask

    task clear_status;
        begin
            axi_write(A_STATUS, 32'h1, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
            `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "STATUS clear is OKAY")
            `CHECK(!irq8, "irq low after the clear")
        end
    endtask

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    // Directed sequence
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
    integer        e;
    integer        e2;
    integer        s;
    integer        base;
    integer        fbase;
    integer        i;
    integer        k;
    integer        ok;
    integer        frozen;
    reg [31:0]     exp32;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    initial begin
        aresetn  = 1'b0;
        awaddr   = 8'h00;
        awvalid  = 1'b0;
        wdata    = 32'h0;
        wstrb    = 4'h0;
        wvalid   = 1'b0;
        bready   = 1'b0;
        araddr   = 8'h00;
        arvalid  = 1'b0;
        rready   = 1'b0;
        lane4_en = 1'b1;
        nonce    = 512'd0;
        ok       = 0;
        repeat (4) @(negedge aclk);
        aresetn = 1'b1;
        @(negedge aclk);

        // 1. Reset values
        `CHECK(awready8 && wready8 && arready8, "ready signals high after reset")
        `CHECK(!bvalid8 && !rvalid8, "no response pending after reset")
        `CHECK(!irq8, "irq low after reset")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h0, OKAY, "CTRL reset value")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h0, OKAY, "LOAD reset value")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "COUNT reset value")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h0, OKAY, "STATUS reset value")

        // 2. LOAD with partial strobes, both channel orders, back-pressure
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'hAABBCCDD, 4'hF, 1, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "LOAD write is OKAY")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'hAABBCCDD, OKAY, "LOAD full write")
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'h11223344, 4'b0101, 2, 3, 2);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "LOAD strobed write is OKAY")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'hAA22CC44, OKAY, "LOAD bytes 0 and 2")
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'h55667788, 4'b1000, 1, 4, 5);
        axi_read(A_LOAD, 4);
        `CHECK_EQ(rd_data, 32'h5522CC44, "LOAD byte 3 read under back-pressure")
        `CHECK_EQ(rd_resp, OKAY, "LOAD read is OKAY")
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'b0000, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "LOAD write with no strobe is OKAY")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h5522CC44, OKAY, "LOAD write with no strobe changes nothing")
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'h00000000, 4'b0110, 2, 0, 1);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h55000044, OKAY, "LOAD bytes 1 and 2 cleared")

        // 3. CTRL write without wstrb[0]
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h00000007, 4'b1110, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "CTRL write without wstrb[0] is OKAY")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h0, OKAY, "CTRL write without wstrb[0] changes nothing")
        idle(10);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "no count started")

        // 4. COUNT is read only; unaligned addresses are unmapped
        axi_write(A_COUNT, 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, SLVERR, "COUNT write is SLVERR")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "COUNT write changes nothing")
        for (i = 0; i < 16; i = i + 1) begin
            if (i[1:0] != 2'b00) begin
                axi_write(i[7:0], 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
                `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, SLVERR, "unaligned write is SLVERR")
                `READ_EXPECT(i[7:0], 32'h0, SLVERR, "unaligned read is zero and SLVERR")
            end
        end
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h0, OKAY, "CTRL unchanged by unaligned writes")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h55000044, OKAY, "LOAD unchanged by unaligned writes")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h0, OKAY, "STATUS unchanged by unaligned writes")

        // 5. Offsets from 0x10 up, ADDR_WIDTH 8 lane only
        lane4_en = 1'b0;
        for (i = 16; i < 256; i = i + 4) begin
            axi_write(i[7:0], 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
            `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, SLVERR, "write at or above 0x10 is SLVERR")
            `READ_EXPECT(i[7:0], 32'h0, SLVERR, "read at or above 0x10 is zero and SLVERR")
        end
        for (i = 17; i < 256; i = i + 30) begin
            axi_write(i[7:0], 32'hFFFFFFFF, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
            `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, SLVERR, "unaligned high write is SLVERR")
            `READ_EXPECT(i[7:0], 32'h0, SLVERR, "unaligned high read is zero and SLVERR")
        end
        lane4_en = 1'b1;
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h0, OKAY, "CTRL not aliased by high offsets")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h55000044, OKAY, "LOAD not aliased by high offsets")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "COUNT not aliased by high offsets")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h0, OKAY, "STATUS not aliased by high offsets")

        // 6. One-shot count of 5, timed to the cycle
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd5, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        expect_rise(e + 5, base + 1);
        `CHECK(irq8, "irq high after the count ends")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h2, OKAY, "EN clears itself after a one-shot")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "COUNT is zero after a one-shot")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "EXPIRED set after a one-shot")
        axi_write(A_STATUS, 32'h0, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "STATUS write of 0 is OKAY")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "writing 0 leaves EXPIRED")
        axi_write(A_STATUS, 32'h1, 4'b1110, 0, 0, 0);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "clear without wstrb[0] leaves EXPIRED")
        `CHECK(irq8, "irq stays high until cleared")
        clear_status;
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h0, OKAY, "EXPIRED cleared")
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        idle(40);
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, base, "no second interrupt from a one-shot")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "COUNT stays zero after a one-shot")

        // One-shot with LOAD 1 and LOAD 0: both end one edge later
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd1, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        expect_rise(e + 1, base + 1);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h2, OKAY, "LOAD 1 one-shot ends")
        clear_status;
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd0, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        expect_rise(e + 1, base + 1);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h2, OKAY, "LOAD 0 one-shot ends")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "LOAD 0 does not wrap")
        clear_status;

        // One-shot of 40 with COUNT read while counting
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd40, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        idle(7);
        axi_read(A_COUNT, 2);
        exp32 = 40 - (rd_edge - 1 - e);
        `CHECK_EQ(rd_data, exp32, "COUNT read while counting")
        `CHECK_EQ(rd_resp, OKAY, "COUNT read is OKAY")
        expect_rise(e + 40, base + 1);
        clear_status;

        // 7. Interrupt enable on a pending expiry
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h1, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        wait_until(e + 5);
        `CHECK(!irq8, "no irq with IE 0")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "EXPIRED set with IE 0")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h0, OKAY, "EN clears itself with IE 0")
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h2, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, base + 1, "irq rises when IE is written 1")
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_edge, wr_edge, "irq rises on the edge IE is written")
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h0, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK(!irq8, "irq low when IE is written 0")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "EXPIRED kept when IE is written 0")
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h2, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK(irq8, "irq high again with IE 1")
        clear_status;

        // 8. Periodic count of 12 over several periods
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd12, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h7, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        for (k = 1; k <= 3; k = k + 1) begin
            expect_rise(e + 12 * k, base + k);
            if (k == 1) begin
                `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h7, OKAY, "EN stays 1 in periodic mode")
            end
            clear_status;
        end
        expect_rise(e + 48, base + 4);
        fbase = irq_fall_cnt;
        // A clear on the edge a count ends: the count end wins
        wait_until(e + 59);
        axi_write(A_STATUS, 32'h1, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_edge, e + 60, "clear lands on the edge a count ends")
        idle(2);
        `CHECK(irq8, "a count end beats a clear")
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_fall_cnt, fbase, "irq did not drop on the colliding clear")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "EXPIRED kept by the count end")
        clear_status;
        expect_rise(e + 72, base + 5);

        // A stop freezes COUNT
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h6, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        s = wr_edge;
        `CHECK((s - e - 72 >= 1) && (s - e - 72 <= 9), "stop lands inside a period")
        frozen = 12 - (s - e - 72);
        exp32 = frozen;
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, exp32, OKAY, "COUNT frozen by the stop")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h6, OKAY, "EN 0 after the stop")
        axi_write(A_COUNT, 32'h12345678, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, SLVERR, "COUNT write is SLVERR while stopped")
        clear_status;
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        idle(40);
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, base, "no count end while stopped")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, exp32, OKAY, "COUNT still frozen")

        // 9. Restart from the stopped state
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd7, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        expect_rise(e + 7, base + 1);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h2, OKAY, "restarted one-shot ends")
        clear_status;

        // 10. Restart while counting
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd30, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        idle(8);
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e2 = wr_edge;
        wait_until(e + 32);
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, base, "the first count did not end after a restart")
        expect_rise(e2 + 30, base + 1);
        clear_status;

        // 11a. EN 1 written on the edge a one-shot ends
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd8, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        wait_until(e + 7);
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h3, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_edge, e + 8, "restart lands on the end edge")
        expect_rise(e + 8, base + 1);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h3, OKAY, "EN 1 wins on the end edge")
        clear_status;
        expect_rise(e + 16, base + 2);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h2, OKAY, "the restarted one-shot ends")
        clear_status;

        // 11b. EN 0 written on the edge a periodic count ends
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h7, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        wait_until(e + 7);
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h6, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_edge, e + 8, "stop lands on the end edge")
        expect_rise(e + 8, base + 1);
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h6, OKAY, "EN 0 wins on the end edge")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'd8, OKAY, "COUNT takes the reload of the end edge")
        idle(30);
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, base + 1, "no count after the stop on the end edge")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h1, OKAY, "EXPIRED set by the count that ended")
        clear_status;

        // 12. Reset during a count, with responses waiting
        axi_write(A_LOAD, 32'd5, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        axi_write(A_CTRL, 32'h7, 4'hF, 0, 0, 0);
        e = wr_edge;
        expect_rise(e + 5, base + 1);
        awaddr  = A_LOAD;
        wdata   = 32'h000000AA;
        wstrb   = 4'hF;
        awvalid = 1'b1;
        wvalid  = 1'b1;
        @(negedge aclk);
        awvalid = 1'b0;
        wvalid  = 1'b0;
        `CHECK(bvalid8, "write response waiting before reset")
        araddr  = A_CTRL;
        arvalid = 1'b1;
        @(negedge aclk);
        arvalid = 1'b0;
        `CHECK(rvalid8, "read response waiting before reset")
        `CHECK(irq8, "interrupt pending before reset")
        aresetn = 1'b0;
        @(negedge aclk);
        `CHECK(!bvalid8 && !rvalid8, "reset drops bvalid and rvalid")
        `CHECK(!irq8, "reset drops irq")
        repeat (2) @(negedge aclk);
        aresetn = 1'b1;
        @(negedge aclk);
        `CHECK(awready8 && wready8 && arready8, "ready signals high after the second reset")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_CTRL, 32'h0, OKAY, "CTRL reset during a count")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h0, OKAY, "LOAD reset during a count")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_COUNT, 32'h0, OKAY, "COUNT reset during a count")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_STATUS, 32'h0, OKAY, "STATUS reset during a count")
        base = irq_rise_cnt;
        idle(30);
        `CHECK_EQ(irq_rise_cnt, base, "no count end after reset")
        `CHECK(!irq8, "irq stays low after reset")

        // 13. A held address does not survive reset
        awaddr  = A_LOAD;
        awvalid = 1'b1;
        @(negedge aclk);
        awvalid = 1'b0;
        `CHECK(!awready8, "address held before reset")
        `CHECK(!bvalid8, "no response for a lone address")
        aresetn = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) @(negedge aclk);
        aresetn = 1'b1;
        @(negedge aclk);
        `CHECK(awready8 && wready8, "held address cleared by reset")
        axi_write(A_STATUS, 32'h0, 4'hF, 2, 2, 0);
        `CHECK_EQ(wr_resp, OKAY, "write after reset pairs with its own address")
        `READ_EXPECT(A_LOAD, 32'h0, OKAY, "no stale write to LOAD")

        // Lanes
        `CHECK(lane_cmp > 0, "the lane comparison ran")
        `CHECK_EQ(lane_mismatch, 0, "ADDR_WIDTH 4 and 8 lanes agree")

        idle(2);
        ok = $value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce);
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

endmodule
